      "side": 1,
      "message": "[error] Line 375: 🔴 `saveContactsLocked()` treats `std::filesystem::permissions(...)` failure as fatal and skips writing entirely (`if (!ec) msgpack::pack(...)`). On platforms/filesystems where chmod-like permission updates are unsupported or restricted, every contact save will fail even though writing/rename would succeed. This can silently break contact metadata sync/persistence. **Fix:** always serialize/write regardless of permission-setting result; either ignore permission errors (log warning) or gate permission changes by platform/feature and keep save path best-effort.",
      "revId": "07b96d98b08a7c5f0f8fc8b75076573ac9308f71",
      "serverId": "1e26b4c1-6b8c-47ff-9df7-501b633d3b5a"
